steps.instructions:
Above `draw()`, add `function seatOf(t) { return t === 'r' ? 0 : 1; }`: the host plays red. A move from another computer could be anything, so below `seatOf` add a check that it is four whole numbers on the board, the way 6.25.1 checked a roll with `floor(r) === r`:

```js
function goodMove(m) {
  if (m === null || m === undefined) return false;
  return isSquare(m.fr, m.fc) && isSquare(m.tr, m.tc);
}
function isSquare(r, c) { return floor(r) === r && floor(c) === c && onBoard(r, c); }
```

Then make `onMove` check before it moves anything: `if (goodMove(m) && seat === seatOf(turn) && winner === '' && isLegal(m.fr, m.fc, m.tr, m.tc)) doMove(m.fr, m.fc, m.tr, m.tc);`. A move that is not four whole numbers, a move from the wrong seat, or one that breaks a rule is now ignored on both computers.
